# The music player of Frantisek Fuka (Fuxoft) that 16 variants carry at $EB50 (kit/mkgame.py --part
# variants/players/fuxoft/fuxoft.json). Format: ../../../../../docs/ann-format.md.
#
# The image: the first 1253 bytes of zyxae's music piece ($EB50-$F034, work/parts/player-fuxoft.bin, written by
# python3 tools/variants_music.py image fuxoft). Every variant has the code at $EB50 and its tune from $F035 (the
# tune's words are absolute addresses, so this player is never moved); tools/variants_music.py lays each variant's
# own bytes over this source (music/player.txt: the variables, the stacks and the noise mask as saved) before the
# tune (music/fuxoft.txt, tools/res_fuxoft.py). No recording runs a variant: every name and description here is from
# the code (tools/ay_render.py runs it to render the WAVs).

@module fuxoft ; Fuxoft's player: three entry vectors, the channel streams with calls and loops, instruments, ornaments
@about Three vectors: MusicStart $EB50 (JP Init) points the three channels at the tune's streams (the words at $F035, $F037, $F039), sets their duration counters to 1, mixer bits to tone off, their call stacks and clears the instruments and ornaments; MusicInit $EB53 (JP Silence) turns the mixer off and writes the AY; MusicPlay $EB56 (JP PlayFrame) plays one frame: ChannelFrame for channels A, B and C, the mixer from their bits, WriteAY.
@about A channel (ChannelFrame, SP on the channel's own stack): when its note's duration runs out, ReadStream reads the stream: a note byte $01-$7F (+ the transposition indexes PeriodTable; 0 is silence) and its duration, or a command $80-$8E through CommandTable (goto, call, repeat, next, noise, mixer, ornament, instrument, transposition, return, tie on, tie off, machine code, noise +, transposition +). Every frame the instrument's volume stream (a volume and its frames, or a short volume for one frame, or $80 goto) and the ornament (a note offset or a period step a frame, or $80 goto) shape the sound. The format is in src/res/music/README.md.

$EB50 c MusicStart ; JP Init: start the tune
$EB53 c MusicInit ; JP Silence: the mixer off
$EB56 c MusicPlay ; JP PlayFrame: play one frame
$EB59 c Init ; Point the channels at the tune's three streams, reset their records and stacks, the noise to 0
$EBAD b InitPad 8 ; 45 zero bytes (unused)
$EBDA c Silence ; The mixer off ($FF into register 7 of AYImage), then WriteAY

$EBE6 b AYImage 8 ; The image of AY registers 0-13 that WriteAY sends (13 first)
$EBF4 b Noise 1 ; The noise period (commands $84 and $8D)
$EBF5 b Channel 1 ; The channel ChannelFrame is working on: 1 A, 2 B, 3 C
$EBF6 w SavedSP 1 ; The caller's stack pointer while ChannelFrame runs on a channel's stack
$EBF8 w WorkPointer 1 ; A work word: the stream pointer while a command or a note is read
$EBFA w StackPointers 3 ; Each channel's stack pointer (its calls and repeats): $EC20, $EC40, $EC60 at Init
$EC00 b Stacks 8 ; The three channels' stacks (32 bytes each, growing down from $EC20, $EC40, $EC60)
$EC60 b ChannelRecords 8 ; The three channels' records (20 bytes each: A $EC60, B $EC74, C $EC88; IX)
> +$00 / +$01 the stream pointer; +$02 the note's frames left; +$03 the mixer bits; +$04 / +$05 the volume stream pointer; +$06 the volume's frames left; +$07 / +$08 the tone period; +$09 the volume; +$0A / +$0B the instrument; +$0C / +$0D the ornament pointer; +$0E flags (bit 0 tie, bit 1 tied note running, bit 2 the note's first frame, bit 3 the ornament adds notes); +$0F the transposition; +$10 / +$11 the ornament; +$12 the note.
$EC74 ChannelB
$EC88 ChannelC
$EC9C w PeriodTable 8 ; The AY tone period of notes 1-84 (A-0 up)

$ED44 c PlayFrame ; Play one frame: ChannelFrame for A, B and C, the mixer from their bits, WriteAY
$ED85 c WriteAY ; Write AYImage to AY registers 13 down to 0
$ED9B c SetAYRegister ; AYImage[D] = A
$EDA4 c ChannelFrameEnd ; Back to the caller's stack (SavedSP) with HL = the channel's stack pointer
$EDB0 c ChannelFrame ; One frame of the channel at IX (A its number, HL its stack pointer): the stream, the volume, the ornament, the AY registers
$EEB8 c SaveStream ; The stream pointer (+$00) = HL
$EEBF c ReadStream ; Read the stream: a note and its duration, or a command (CommandTable)
$EF3C c StreamCommand ; A command byte $80-$8E: jump through CommandTable
$EF52 w CommandTable 8 ; The 15 command routines ($80-$8E)
$EF70 c CommandGoto ; $80 w: goto
$EF7C c CommandCall ; $81 w: call a sub-stream (the return address on the channel's stack)
$EF8A c CommandRepeat ; $82 n: repeat up to $83 n times
$EF94 c CommandNext ; $83: the end of a repeat
$EFA6 c CommandNoise ; $84 n: the noise period
$EFB1 c CommandMixer ; $85 n: the channel's mixer bits
$EFBC c CommandInstrument ; $87 w: the instrument
$EFCC c CommandTranspose ; $88 n: the transposition
$EFD7 c CommandReturn ; $89: return from a call
$EFDE c CommandOrnament ; $86 w: the ornament
$EFEE c CommandTie ; $8A: tie on (a note keeps the volume stream running)
$EFFC c CommandUntie ; $8B: tie off
$F00A c CommandCode ; $8C w: call machine code
$F017 c CommandNoiseAdd ; $8D n: noise += n (AND the noise mask: the operand at $F01C, $1F or $0F in the variants)
$F027 c CommandTransposeAdd ; $8E n: transposition += n
